# Figma Design Workflow

## Design source of truth

- **Live site CSS**: `:root` variables in `index.html` (lines ~12–30).
- **Figma tokens**: `design/figma-tokens.json` — import into Figma via [Tokens Studio](https://tokens.studio/) plugin.
- When tokens change in Figma, update both `design/figma-tokens.json` and `:root` in `index.html`.

## Figma file structure (recommended pages)

1. **🎨 Design System** — colors, typography, buttons, stat cards, nav
2. **🏠 Public Site** — Hero, About, Products grid, Contact, Footer (1440 / 768 / 375 frames)
3. **⚙️ Admin** — optional; admin UI also lives in `index.html`

## Implementing Figma → code

- All public + admin UI stays in **single** `index.html` — never split CSS/JS out.
- Map Figma colors to existing `--*` CSS variables; do not introduce new hex values without updating tokens.
- Fonts: **Playfair Display** (headings), **DM Sans** (body) — already loaded from Google Fonts.
- User shares Figma link or screenshot → match spacing, radius, and hierarchy from the mockup.
- Content text: prefer Admin **Site Editor** + `site-content.json` for copy; use code only for layout/CSS.

## Sections to mirror in Figma

| Figma frame | HTML anchor |
|-------------|-------------|
| Hero | `#home` / `.hero` |
| About | `#about-section` |
| Products | `#products-section` |
| Contact | `#contact-section` |
| Footer | `.site-footer` |

## Do not

- Export React/Vue from Figma — implement manually in `index.html`.
- Change deploy model (Netlify + GitHub `main` auto-deploy).
